---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="RentEarth"
  description="A turn-based 4X built schema first: one set of definitions the client, the servers and this site all read from."
>
  <section class="statement bleed">
    <h1>A 4X built <span class="mark">backwards</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most strategy games start with a prototype and grow a data model around it
      once the systems stop moving. RentEarth starts from the definitions — the
      things a turn is made of — and builds outward from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ul class="claims bleed">
    <li class="claim">
      <h2>Explore, expand, exploit, exterminate</h2>
      <p>
        Turn-based, in the Civilization tradition. The four verbs are settled.
        The map, the eras and the win conditions are not, and this site will not
        pretend otherwise until they are.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="claim">
      <h2>One definition, four languages</h2>
      <p>
        Items, spells, quests, dialogue and rarity live in Protobuf. TypeScript,
        Rust, C# and Python are generated from it. Rename a field and every one
        of them fails to build in the same minute.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="claim">
      <h2>A turn is a contract</h2>
      <p>
        A 4X accumulates state for hundreds of turns, so a save from an early
        build has to keep meaning something. Defining the wire format before the
        systems is what makes that possible rather than aspirational.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="claim">
      <h2>Built where you can watch</h2>
      <p>
        The monorepo is public. The commits, the schemas and the mistakes are
        readable while the game is still being decided.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <section class="ledger bleed">
    <div class="ledger-inner">
      <h2>Decided so far</h2>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Genre</dt>
          <dd>4X, turn-based</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Systems modelled</dt>
          <dd>items · spells · quests · dialogue · rarity</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Schema registry</dt>
          <dd>14 definitions across 6 domains</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Generated targets</dt>
          <dd>TypeScript · Rust · C# · Python</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Map, eras, victory</dt>
          <dd>undecided</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Playable build</dt>
          <dd>none</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close bleed">
    <p>
      There is nothing to play yet and no date to promise. If watching a strategy
      game get built from its data model outward is interesting to you, the work
      is public.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="https://github.com/KBVE/workspace" rel="noopener">
      Read the repository
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>
